<DocsPageTitle Path="Components/Jumbotron">
    Blazorise Jumbotron component
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    Give a page introduction or featured message a prominent place.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Use the <Code>Jumbotron</Code> component for a landing page introduction, announcement, or other content that needs more emphasis than the surrounding page.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Structure
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A <Code>Jumbotron</Code> can contain a title, a subtitle, and other featured content.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsAnatomy Label="Jumbotron component anatomy">
    <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="Jumbotron" Description="Contains the featured content.">
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="JumbotronTitle" Description="The main heading." />
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="JumbotronSubtitle" Description="An optional supporting heading." />
    </DocsAnatomyRegion>
</DocsAnatomy>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Examples
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Basic">
        <Paragraph>
            Jumbotron is a full width <Anchor To="docs/components/card" Title="Link to card component">card</Anchor> that is usually displayed at the top of the page, sometimes also referred to as a "Hero component".
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            The jumbotron color should be only slightly off the background of the page to make your design feel "light".
        </Paragraph>
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="BasicJumbotronExample" Outlined FullWidth>
